<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.781 µm on a Holocene Canis lupus (MDCK) apical patch — MorphoEval overall 81.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 integrates the Schnakenberg system so that the determinant formula for k_c lands on 1.781 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma, domain 14.248 µm = 8 wavelengths). Continuum versus coarse finite-difference dispersion curves give Pearson r = 0.9935 (RMSE 1.002). The saturated Fourier peak sits at 0.976 k_c. The growth GIF is 16 frames at 640×480; its last frame is the canonical micrograph modulated by the activator (CV similarity 96.0 against that micrograph). Specimen nearest-neighbour spacing is 8.94 px and is not converted to micrometres. The diffusivity sweep, equal-diffusion figure, gamma=0 panel, and KS area test are implemented but gated off (REMEDIATION_PASS = 1), so this pass does not score them as done. Overall 81.6/100 (faithfulness 80.6, reproducibility 84.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 68, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/canis_lupus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 686761 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 747326cd4a188994ab07bd96e5161cd1c806625536239387a42749b0c359f73f (sha256 747326cd4a188994ab07bd96e5161cd1c806625536239387a42749b0c359f73f), spec_fingerprint 32ef3bbb738079fa3f2ca196a6ebf3a8f753f2f1e9cf9f5d0d12a208ec2f4990. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 62f18d9df76b5263186739999d39e30372650ea68bead990595950ce9e6644ae; artifact_sha256: 747326cd4a188994ab07bd96e5161cd1c806625536239387a42749b0c359f73f; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/canis_lupus_turing_wavelength_s0/canis_lupus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=d16ba21863080c9e..., datasets/canis_lupus_turing_wavelength_s0/canis_lupus_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=8dd4a5b3caa19a6f...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing dispersion relation and a finite unstable band of wavenumbers | Schnakenberg trimolecular kinetics | Murray coat pre-patterns are centimetre-scale | MDCK cells are a polarized canine epithelium | Domestic-dog black coat is a beta-defensin allele, not a measured micrometre wavelength; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.10, b=1.10, gamma=40, D_u=0.8, D_v=9.6 chosen so lambda_c = 1.781e-6 m | Time unit of 1 s used only to quote an equivalent diffusivity | Periodic 8-wavelength patch as one apical face; transfer_boundary: Murray 1981 is not a measurement of Canis lupus at 1.8 µm | The gallery micrograph has no scale bar; does_not_claim: That Holocene wolf coat spots have wavelength 1.781 µm | That each histological polygon is one Turing spot | That a second assessor scored this pass." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Execute sweep_diffusion_ratio, plot lambda_c against D_v/D_u, and write the sweep into the measurement sidecar (set REMEDIATION_PASS = 2).'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Run the equal-diffusion and gamma=0 integrations and show their activator standard deviations next to the patterned regime.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Compute the median-normalised two-sample KS statistic between specimen domain areas and simulated activator-peak areas, with value not equal to the reference.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Independent second assessor was not run. Left open; this pass is builder-scored only.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Keep the explicit statement that specimen spacing is in pixels and is not a 1.781 µm measurement once the pass-2 panels replace the text block.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.16e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
